# repo-scan-quoted-examples — made-up addresses that outside reviews quote,
# each allowed only in the file that quotes it.
#
# An outside review shows a scanner hole with an invented address, such as
# "anything@" at an organisation's domain. Kept verbatim, the review fails the
# scan. Listed in repo-scan-public-addresses, the address would pass in every
# file, though nobody published it (outside reviews of 05f5aef, 2026-10-21).
# So each line here is
#
#   <path of the quoting file>  <address exactly as quoted>
#
# and devtools/repo-scan lets the address through only while no other tracked
# file contains it. These are NOT anyone's addresses. Never list a real one
# here: a published address belongs in repo-scan-public-addresses, and an
# unpublished one belongs nowhere.

